It states an exact-rational certificate for the one-sample matroid prophet model, obtained
by evaluating a published closed form at the exact rational point B = (261/256)^256 with
three analysis constants tightened, and by checking every side condition as an exact
rational inequality.

The mathematical foundation is OpenAI's "One Sample Suffices for Matroid Prophet
Inequalities against an Almighty Adversary", OpenAI Math release preprint, 23 September
2026, commit 1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a; that repository's root license is
Apache 2.0. The analysis constants and scalar chain are Ryan Shea's refinements, commit
8cd1395994596d89ad20c2af8b69dab8e3402ee1 (github.com/shea256/open-math-problems), also
Apache 2.0. The closed form, the conservative evaluation B > 141 and the incumbent
certificate C141 are Qiuyu Chen (Euler), "An exact rational certificate for one-sample
matroid prophet inequalities", bound-111 of github.com/canghaimeng/openai-math-improvement,
17 October 2026.

This repository's own contribution is the evaluation point, the refined analysis constants,
and check_C.py. No upstream source text or code is redistributed here; the conditions are
transcribed with citation in PROOF.md. These acknowledgments do not imply endorsement or
independent review by any of the parties named above.
